/* ============================================================================
   t-critical-values.epher -- t cut points for common levels and df

   The t distribution cut points t such that P(T <= t) equals the
   probability in `p` with the given degrees of freedom, from the builtin
   invt (guide 1.20). The 97.5th percentile with 10 df is the 2.2281 of
   two-sided 95 percent intervals. As the degrees of freedom grow the t
   approaches the standard normal, so the last line compares invt with
   60 df against invnorm(0.975) = 1.96.

   Run it from a terminal:
     Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/statistics/distributions/t-critical-values.epher
     Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\statistics\distributions\t-critical-values.epher"
     macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/statistics/distributions/t-critical-values.epher
   In the REPL:             load one of the paths above
   Web/desktop:             paste the whole file into the entry, press Enter
   Everything also works line by line in the TUI.

   No knobs: the levels and degrees of freedom below are the demonstration.
   ============================================================================ */

// ---- the cut points -------------------------------------------------------------------
print("invt(0.975, 10):", invt(0.975, 10))    // the 95% two-sided t with 10 df
print("invt(0.95, 20):", invt(0.95, 20))      // the 90% two-sided t with 20 df
print("invt(0.995, 30):", invt(0.995, 30))    // the 99% two-sided t with 30 df

// ---- each cut point fed back through the cdf comes back to its probability ------------
print("tcdf(invt(0.975, 10), 10):", tcdf(invt(0.975, 10), 10))

// ---- the approach to the normal: 60 df is already near 1.96 ------------------------------
print("invt(0.975, 60):", invt(0.975, 60))
print("invnorm(0.975):", invnorm(0.975))

/* ---- expected output ----
= invt(0.975, 10): 2.22813885199
= invt(0.95, 20): 1.72471824292
= invt(0.995, 30): 2.74999565357
= tcdf(invt(0.975, 10), 10): 0.975
= invt(0.975, 60): 2.00029782202
= invnorm(0.975): 1.95996398454
*/